Deosil is a neighborhood of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. The one robber taken alive after the ambush at a rest-stop gas station said his crew had bought their guns, marked with [[Org/Sable and Suns/index|Sable and Suns]] tokens, there from a man named Lark.

Deosil is inland, with no direct connection to the river, and its industry is mostly factories turning out home appliances and toys rather than the docks of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/index|Sableclutch]] and [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]]. It has little housing and little service trade. A factory at 414 Anchor Street, one part a single-floor warehouse and one part two floors, was the front for [[People/Sbrtlby Jotes|Sbrtlby Jotes]]'s drug ring; the Party killed him and his henchmen there.

The works at 414 Anchor Street, registered under Sbrtlby's name, were brought down when the Party and the [[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anouk Marchal|Marchal]] twins left it: the building folded in on itself and damaged nothing around it.
